title: 'pallet-child-bounties: use saturating_add for unlock_at'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes an arithmetic overflow in `award_child_bounty`. The pending payout
    `unlock_at` block number was computed with a plain `+`, which can overflow
    (and in release builds silently wrap) when the treasury block number is
    large or when `BountyDepositPayoutDelay` is configured to a large value.
    The addition now uses `saturating_add`, so `unlock_at` saturates at the
    maximum block number instead of wrapping, keeping the payout lock far in
    the future rather than unlocking immediately.

crates:
- name: pallet-child-bounties
  bump: patch
